# What must never enter a build context.
#
# THIS FILE IS A SECURITY CONTROL, not an optimisation. Without it, `docker
# build .` uploads `data/` — which holds the license signing key, the session
# key and the pepper — into the daemon, where one careless `COPY . .` in any
# future Dockerfile stage would bake it into a published image layer.
#
# It is also what makes the frontend builds correct at all: `COPY site/ ./`
# would otherwise overwrite the container's freshly-installed `node_modules`
# with the host's (built for a different platform), and pnpm aborts with
# ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY rather than silently using them.
#
# Measured on this repo the day it was added: 726 MB of `data/`, 384 MB of
# `node_modules/`, 53 MB of `server/bin/`.

# --- runtime state: KEY MATERIAL. Never in a build context. ---
# The same pattern .gitignore uses, and for the same reason: every tool that
# takes a --data-dir invents another one of these.
data/
data-*/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
diagnostics/

# --- deployment secrets ---
infra/deploy.env
infra/.release.env

# --- dependencies: installed inside the image, per platform ---
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# --- build output: rebuilt inside the image ---
server/bin/
site/dist/
spa/dist/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# --- things no stage reads ---
.git/
.github/
.claude/
mod/
docs/
plans/
site/e2e/
**/.DS_Store
*.md
!scripts/*.md

# NOT ignored, and each is needed by a stage:
#   server/          Dockerfile.catlogd
#   site/ spa/       Dockerfile.nginx (minus the exclusions above)
#   scripts/precompress.mjs
#   infra/nginx/*    Dockerfile.nginx
